SUMMARY:HANDEL + HENDRIX With Dither\, R.B. Schlather\, and Ruckus
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:Two radical innovators. Three centuries apart. One evening. Han
 del and Hendrix lived in adjacent homes in London's Mayfair district — s
 eparated by 250 years\, divided by a single wall\, now joined as the Hande
 l Hendrix House museum. In honor of the museum's 25th anniversary\, Nation
 al Sawdust and Handel Hendrix House America present an evening that brings
  these two radical innovators into direct confrontation. Electric guitar q
 uartet Dither open the evening with newly commissioned works that channel 
 Hendrix's experimental language. Director R.B. Schlather and early music e
 nsemble Ruckus then bring Handel's Deidamia — his final opera — to cha
 mber scale in National Sawdust's intimate acoustic space.\nhttps://www.nat
 ionalsawdust.org/event/handel-hendrix-with-dither-r-b-schlather-and-ruckus
 -12-5-26\nFrom Pushpin NYC: https://pushpin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/handel-hendrix-with-dither-r-b-sc
 hlather-and-ruckus-12-5-26
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4a3bbe52772e80316e0d096952b2f5b47fa72e5d@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261207
SUMMARY:LPR Presents: S. Carey
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:S. Carey is the moniker of Eau Claire\, Wisconsin-based multi-i
 nstrumentalist\, songwriter\, and producer Sean Carey\, commonly recognize
 d as the drummer\, backing vocalist\, and second longest serving member of
  Bon Iver. Over the past decade and a half\, Carey has fostered his flouri
 shing solo career via themes of nature and sustainability\, songwriting bu
 ilt from jazz beginnings\, and heartfelt\, emotive lyricism. His latest re
 lease\, Watercress\, adds to a discography of four full-length releases\, 
 two EPs\, and countless collaborations\, including Unbound with Bizhiki an
 d Shadowlands with John Raymond.\nhttps://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/lp
 r-presents-s-carey\nFrom Pushpin NYC: https://pushpin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/lpr-presents-s-carey
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fc16bc49793c741d53703399dfc898c5f02f3bd7@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
SUMMARY:Hildegard Commission Concert 2026
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:The Hildegard Commission Concert returns with groundbreaking pr
 emieres from our four winners\, today’s most exciting rising composers
 —che buford\, Līva Blūma\, Fjóla Evans\, and Maria-Eduarda Mendes Mar
 tin—along with works from our four brilliant finalists. The namesake of 
 our commission\, 12th-century mystic Hildegard von Bingen\, used vivid\, i
 ntricate miniature drawings in her prophetic books to bring complex spirit
 ual visions to life. For this year’s commission\, our winners have compo
 sed music that directly responds to a distinct illustration from Hildegard
 's codices. These historic images will be brought to life through dynamic 
 animations and projections from a visionary visual designer\, transforming
  the performance space into an interactive ecosystem of sight and sound. S
 tep into a multi-sensory\, immersive environment inspired by the extraordi
 nary legacy of the 12th-century mystic Hildegard von Bingen.\nhttps://www.
 nationalsawdust.org/event/hildegard-commission-concert-2026\nFrom Pushpin 
 NYC: https://pushpin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/hildegard-commission-concert-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:61b574a6a2bbb1012c2959f36395e936bb601629@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
SUMMARY:inti figgis-vizueta’s Music for Transitions with Andrew Yee and R
 othko String Quartet
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:Composer inti figgis-vizueta presents her 2026 debut record Mus
 ic for Transitions\, with a performance featuring GRAMMY Award-winning cel
 list Andrew Yee and the Germany-based Rothko String Quartet. Exploring Ind
 igenous heritage and trans identity through playful\, ecstatic soundscapes
 \, the album exemplifies figgis-vizueta’s deep commitment to personal li
 beration through group improvisation. Recurring themes of land\, wind\, ri
 vers\, and cosmology are framed by constant musical transformation in what
  composer George Lewis calls “the dynamics of the decolonial.”\nhttps:
 //www.nationalsawdust.org/event/inti-figgis-vizuetas-music-for-transitions
 -with-andrew-yee-and-rothko-string-quartet\nFrom Pushpin NYC: https://push
 pin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/inti-figgis-vizuetas-music-for-tr
 ansitions-with-andrew-yee-and-rothko-string-quartet
END:VEVENT
