UID:8218eb03d38ae92e26ae5297d4d1e1dd6b1902c0@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270129
SUMMARY:Kyle Sanna: Everything Again Is New (Live Coding with Ensemble)
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:Composer\, guitarist\, and live coder Kyle Sanna presents the f
 ull premiere of Everything Again Is New\, a set of algorithmic composition
 s for electronics and ensemble centered on themes of cyclical regeneration
  and renewal. Joined by Kinan Azmeh (clarinet\, bass clarinet)\, Lily Holg
 ate (violin)\, Nathan Koci (accordion)\, and Marika Hughes (cello)\, Sanna
  (guitar\, electronics) will use code to reanimate recorded fragments of h
 is own chamber orchestra work\, all while projections show the generative 
 process itself\, as text becomes sound.\nhttps://www.nationalsawdust.org/e
 vent/kyle-sanna-everything-again-is-new-live-coding-with-ensemble-1-28-202
 7\nFrom Pushpin NYC: https://pushpin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/kyle-sanna-everything-again-is-ne
 w-live-coding-with-ensemble-1-28-2027
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bc6affc7755b44c41addb2c42a33ca03935e5a8b@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270203
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270204
SUMMARY:Emily Wells - Mirror Father - a workshop performance
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:For the past several years Emily Wells has been knocking on the
  door of an opera. Each year the door cracks open a little wider\, the sto
 ry gets louder\, and the collaborators become clearer. This opera is a sto
 ry about remaking the past in order to understand\, and perhaps change\, t
 he future. It’s a conversation between a “mirror father” living the 
 life he might have lived had he come out in the early 80s instead of livin
 g a closeted life\, and his “phantom daughter” who he begins dreaming 
 about. The two discover overlays: their queerness\, their art\, their rela
 tion to capital and its effects on community. At the center is each one's 
 desire to have a child but choosing not to due to their fears of the end o
 f the world\, his AIDS\, hers climate catastrophe.\nhttps://www.nationalsa
 wdust.org/event/emily-wells-mirror-father-a-workshop-performance\nFrom Pus
 hpin NYC: https://pushpin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/emily-wells-mirror-father-a-works
 hop-performance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2d79753c3fe368fc06df2c322b6cb996ec2beebe@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261128T153847Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270207
SUMMARY:BB Wisely
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:Hark! Behold: SLEDDING\, the first full-length album from BB WI
 SELY. You might listen to this album and think it sounds unusually seasone
 d for a debut\, and you’d be dead on. That’s because the relationships
  between the three humans of this trio date back to the early 2000’s\, w
 hen iPod’s had wheels and arguing about AI was something that happened i
 n a Spielberg chat room. The musical and personal developments between Ben
 jamin Lazar Davis\, Bridget Kearney and Will Graefe have pushed forth sinc
 e those days both in overlaps with each other and on their own circuitous 
 career paths\, but never has this trio acted as a unified whole until this
  very record: SLEDDING is here and it is one fully baked potato.\nhttps://
 www.nationalsawdust.org/event/bb-wisely-2-06-2027\nFrom Pushpin NYC: https
 ://pushpin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/bb-wisely-2-06-2027
END:VEVENT
